WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.502
-Alright. Thank you. Thank you,
thank you, thank you. Alright.

00:00:03.502 --> 00:00:04.870
Turn up, turn up.
Gang, gang, gang.

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:07.240
Okay. Okay. Thank you.

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:10.877
Thank you. Man, I been
in therapy for one year now.

00:00:10.877 --> 00:00:12.445
Whoo! And I'm excited, man.

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:14.380
I'm trying to get my homies
to go to therapy, too,

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:16.249
but every time I tell them,
they like, "Nah, man,

00:00:16.249 --> 00:00:18.418
just do push-ups."

00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:21.654
[ Laughter ]

00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:25.124
Which is cool, but, like, after
I'm done, I'm still crying.

00:00:25.124 --> 00:00:26.493
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.493 --> 00:00:29.261
I just have a bigger chest.

00:00:29.261 --> 00:00:32.998
I got tears running down my
chest like a sad D'Angelo video.

00:00:32.998 --> 00:00:36.402
♪ How does it feel ♪

00:00:36.402 --> 00:00:38.371
[ Imitating
high-pitched sobbing ]

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:39.973
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.973 --> 00:00:42.208
You don't want to see that.

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:43.409
Therapy's great, though.

00:00:43.409 --> 00:00:45.378
Every time I tell my therapist
my issues,

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:49.448
she gives me an understanding
moan like, "Mm-hmm.

00:00:49.448 --> 00:00:51.851
Mm-hmm."

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:53.620
Like my issues are dessert.

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:55.788
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.788 --> 00:00:57.590
"Here's my apple anxiety pie."

00:00:57.590 --> 00:00:59.325
"Mmm.

00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:02.394
That's good."

00:01:02.394 --> 00:01:05.130
"Here's my depression
blueberry muffin."

00:01:05.130 --> 00:01:07.700
"Mm, why you so sad?"

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.535
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.535 --> 00:01:11.671
"Your depression
just needed sugar."

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:12.905
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.905 --> 00:01:16.176
Of course I'm depressed.
I'm a Millennial.

00:01:16.176 --> 00:01:18.911
I'm going to be renting forever.

00:01:18.911 --> 00:01:20.579
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:20.579 --> 00:01:23.049
Forever.

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:25.218
You know, I'm not mad
at Baby Boomers.

00:01:25.218 --> 00:01:26.886
I'm just jealous
that they got here first

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:29.122
and bought all the land for $40.

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:31.924
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.924 --> 00:01:33.593
Like, there's nothing for us.

00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:36.296
Nothing. I checked Amazon.
We ain't got nothing.

00:01:36.296 --> 00:01:37.397
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.397 --> 00:01:38.631
But that's alright, though.

00:01:38.631 --> 00:01:40.099
Feel like there's
gonna be change,

00:01:40.099 --> 00:01:41.467
'cause a lot
of the Baby Boomers,

00:01:41.467 --> 00:01:44.037
they in the back of the computer
store asking for our help.

00:01:44.037 --> 00:01:45.371
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:47.474
That's where we get change.

00:01:47.474 --> 00:01:51.311
They all back there, "Can you
help me reset my password?"

00:01:51.311 --> 00:01:53.479
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.479 --> 00:01:55.614
"You gonna help me
with a house?"

00:01:55.614 --> 00:01:59.285
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:00.920
Hmm?

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:03.589
[ Applause ]

00:02:03.589 --> 00:02:06.492
Still got to get it, Grandma.

00:02:06.492 --> 00:02:09.562
You gonna co-sign this mortgage?

00:02:09.562 --> 00:02:12.531
No? Well, I don't know
passwords. I don't know.

00:02:12.531 --> 00:02:14.567
I don't even work here. Next!"

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:17.036
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:20.173
People don't realize this --

00:02:20.173 --> 00:02:22.741
Like, alright, anybody
that's 21 and older,

00:02:22.741 --> 00:02:23.810
you ever realize this?

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:27.814
Like, we were all
born in the 1900s.

00:02:27.814 --> 00:02:29.248
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.248 --> 00:02:32.118
Like, the people in the 1800s
are all dead.

00:02:32.118 --> 00:02:33.586
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:35.254
It's just us.

00:02:35.254 --> 00:02:38.424
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:44.464
Like, I feel like I'm starting
to sound like my mom.

00:02:44.464 --> 00:02:46.499
Like, I remember anything in
the news with Michael Jackson,

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:48.067
she would defend him like,
"Well, you know what?

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:50.336
I like Michael
with the big nose.

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:52.004
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.004 --> 00:02:54.274
Michael with the big nose and
the afro and the bell bottoms,

00:02:54.274 --> 00:02:56.342
that's the only
Michael Jackson I know."

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:57.810
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.810 --> 00:03:00.712
I say the same thing
just for Kanye West.

00:03:00.712 --> 00:03:03.883
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:09.655 --> 00:03:12.858
"You know Yeezy
with the Louis Vuitton book bag

00:03:12.858 --> 00:03:14.327
and the braces?

00:03:14.327 --> 00:03:17.096
That's my Yeezy.

00:03:17.096 --> 00:03:19.198
That's the only Yeezy I know."

00:03:19.198 --> 00:03:20.733
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:23.269
Nah, I love Kanye. [ Chuckles ]

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:24.703
And we all miss traveling.

00:03:24.703 --> 00:03:26.572
And two years ago,
I was in Paris.

00:03:26.572 --> 00:03:29.041
And I'm not bragging,
I just have to give a shout-out

00:03:29.041 --> 00:03:31.377
to my credit card limit
for extending itself.

00:03:31.377 --> 00:03:33.145
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.145 --> 00:03:34.714
You ever had that? Like, word?

00:03:34.714 --> 00:03:36.982
You gonna give me more money
off the money I still owe you?

00:03:36.982 --> 00:03:39.952
Turn up!

00:03:39.952 --> 00:03:42.622
We out!

00:03:42.622 --> 00:03:45.157
I don't get that when rappers
like, "Get money. Get money."

00:03:45.157 --> 00:03:46.559
No, get credit.

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:48.461
[ Laughter ]

00:03:48.461 --> 00:03:51.164
Get credit, use it, then die.

00:03:51.164 --> 00:03:52.364
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.364 --> 00:03:53.900
Get out of there.

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:56.436
[ Applause ]

00:03:59.238 --> 00:04:01.306
I'm a Millennial.
All I'm passing down to my kids

00:04:01.306 --> 00:04:03.742
is knowledge and debt.

00:04:03.742 --> 00:04:06.045
"Here's my student loans.

00:04:06.045 --> 00:04:08.413
and the people in the family
that I owe."

00:04:08.413 --> 00:04:10.516
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:16.321 --> 00:04:18.658
Minimal payment, baby.

00:04:18.658 --> 00:04:20.759
Minimal payment.

00:04:20.759 --> 00:04:22.361
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:22.361 --> 00:04:24.731
I'm Nore Davis!
Thank you so much.

